aredness","s4c67011495a28c":"A simple test environment.","s7eacd648ed0ebe":"GPU: A40 * 2","s2a52498fa68b2f":"K8s: v1.23.17","sf4bff25ee245ef":"HAMI: v2.3.13","s341d2c75e76203":"GPU Environment","s6cbed0d1ad3014":"Install GPU driver, Container Runte etc. with GPU-Operator","sec3c5faefbd908":"Then install HAMi, reference-- ","sf407d58280326e":"The previous article, Open Source vGPU Program: HAMi to achieve fine particle size GPU splits","scb060950e7359f":"Test Environment","sb546b32e14b7d3":"Just use the Torch mirror and start Pod as a test environment.","sa1aeb5b0ce7a2d":"docker pull pytorch/pytorch:2.4.1-cuda11.8-cudnn9-runtime\n","s04f0661896efe0":"Test script","s0c15a01427c205":"You can use Examples as a test script from PyTorch","se41b76e8ac94dd":"This is a trained Demo, which prints every step of the way, and the lower it gets, the longer it takes.","s8e7b16d149c474":"The specifics are also simple:","s135458747de7bb":"Project Cloning First","s0d4e971e3793a7":"git ","sb5d61dc89a35d2":"clone","sf2757003f274e4":" https://github.com/pytorch/examples.git\n","s2ad84ef37b4d01":"Then start the GPU task.","s21e721c35a5823":"cd","s1416e5bdf39ece":" /mnt/imagenet/\npython main.py -a resnet18 --dummy\n","s6defafa2caa653":"Configure","s63c66f01ca7765":"Need to inject environmental variables into Pod ","se32055f1c6e12c":"GPU_CORE_UTILIZATION_POLICY=force","seb0d5884569b39":"。","s164a33e90b5aec":"This environment variable is used to control the limitations of GPU Core usage, and common values are available ","s37a8eec1ce1968":"default","sc1e0cced307af1":"(Default, limit access only when multiple Pods use the same GPU) and ","s32500d7500ce07":"force","s4be58fef5f0a16":"(Forced limit for all other Pods, whether or not there is any other Pod) with default value as ","sc50109da4b3561":"By default, the limitation strategy is that when the GPU has only one Pod in use, it will not be used as a restriction.","s7d2c4f6eb663e3":"Note: It's an optimisation to increase GPU utilization, an